  The man who should have been her father violated a sacred rule. As a result, he was forced to give up that right, and sever all the ties of blood.

//　それは必ずしも父の本意ではなかった。
//　しかしこの世の法が、父の父たる事を認めなかった。
  That was not, I know, at all what he wanted, but the laws of man would not allow him to take up the mantle of fatherhood.

